00:58:35.690 --> 00:58:37.650
I mean, I was so sold on that.

1255
00:58:37.830 --> 00:58:38.050
Yeah.

1256
00:58:38.290 --> 00:58:39.170
No, he was not.

1257
00:58:39.350 --> 00:58:40.390
He was just off camera.

1258
00:58:40.710 --> 00:58:47.210
But incidentally, I would like to point out that our sound team was nominated for an Emmy

1259
00:58:47.210 --> 00:58:52.310
for Outstanding Sound Mixing for a Comedy or Drama Series Half Hour for this episode.

1260
00:58:52.310 --> 00:58:53.570
Well, they deserve it.

1261
00:58:53.690 --> 00:58:54.070
I know.

1262
00:58:54.210 --> 00:58:55.910
That really sounded like he was up there.

1263
00:58:56.050 --> 00:58:57.450
And all the flushing and everything.

1264
00:58:58.470 --> 00:59:01.770
Well, Michael's going to call his mom and talk in code.

1265
00:59:01.930 --> 00:59:05.030
Jenna, much in the way that you and I talk in code, he's really bad at it.

1266
00:59:05.130 --> 00:59:06.130
It's so obvious.

1267
00:59:06.350 --> 00:59:06.830
It's so obvious.

1268
00:59:07.030 --> 00:59:09.270
He says, Mom, they're getting on my nerves.

1269
00:59:09.490 --> 00:59:10.810
R thinks he's too good to be here.

1270
00:59:10.890 --> 00:59:12.890
And P is not as much fun without Jim.

1271
00:59:13.370 --> 00:59:15.370
And then he's like, Mom, I got to go.

1272
00:59:15.510 --> 00:59:16.670
P's being a giant bee.

1273
00:59:17.230 --> 00:59:18.490
This is us, lady.

1274
00:59:18.950 --> 00:59:25.050
Well, this whole thing is going to end with Pam and Ryan bickering over the computer.

1275
00:59:25.490 --> 00:59:28.750
I mean, they get in a huge fight over who gets to use it.

1276
00:59:29.210 --> 00:59:35.370
And at eight minutes and 20 seconds at the end of this scene, the camera pushes in on Michael.

1277
00:59:35.630 --> 00:59:37.530
He's standing in front of the whiteboard.

1278
00:59:37.830 --> 00:59:42.090
And written on the whiteboard is a quote that says,

1279
00:59:42.310 --> 00:59:45.550
You miss 100% of the shots you don't take.

1280
00:59:45.550 --> 00:59:48.170
Wayne Gretzky, Michael Scott.

1281
00:59:49.550 --> 00:59:52.350
As if Wayne Gretzky is part of the quote.

1282
00:59:52.590 --> 00:59:53.170
Yes.

1283
00:59:53.510 --> 00:59:53.690
Right?

1284
00:59:53.970 --> 00:59:58.190
Michael Scott is quoting himself, quoting Wayne Gretzky.

1285
00:59:58.710 --> 01:00:00.730
Justin Spitzer wrote that joke.

1286
01:00:01.290 --> 01:00:06.030
Gene and Lee both brought it up saying it was one of their favorite parts of the episode.

1287
01:00:06.450 --> 01:00:08.750
Like, I see that meme all the time.

1288
01:00:08.910 --> 01:00:09.490
Oh, yeah.

1289
01:00:09.670 --> 01:00:10.430
It's so brilliant.

1290
01:00:10.430 --> 01:00:17.830
If you Google Wayne Gretzky's quote, a Michael Scott version with his picture comes up.

1291
01:00:17.950 --> 01:00:18.470
It's crazy.

1292
01:00:18.750 --> 01:00:20.250
Well, why don't we take a break?

1293
01:00:20.470 --> 01:00:27.890
And when we come back, we still have to discuss the pancake luncheon and Dwight and Andy's rivalry.

1294
01:00:28.270 --> 01:00:32.710
And Jim maybe finally figuring out what a rundown is.

1295
01:00:32.710 --> 01:00:36.410
And also, a scene where maybe Jim has disappeared.

1296
01:00:36.610 --> 01:00:37.770
Where has he gone?

1297
01:00:37.970 --> 01:00:39.170
You might have the answer.

1298
01:00:39.430 --> 01:00:40.010
Oh, wow.

1299
01:00:40.210 --> 01:00:42.330
Oh, I also have a sunglasses thing.

1300
01:00:42.530 --> 01:00:43.930
Oh, and I do too.

1301
01:00:44.150 --> 01:00:45.870
There's so much to come back for.

1302
01:00:55.240 --> 01:00:56.120
We're back.

1303
01:00:56.540 --> 01:01:01.700
Dwight is going to approach Andy about his obvious attraction to Aaron.

1304
01:01:01.700 --> 01:01:07.780
In only a way that Dwight would, about tingly feelings and blood flow to places.

1305
01:01:08.720 --> 01:01:09.000
Yes.

1306
01:01:09.240 --> 01:01:14.000
But he also confesses that he has his own feelings for Aaron.

1307
01:01:14.620 --> 01:01:15.000
Mm-hmm.

1308
01:01:15.420 --> 01:01:19.380
And they sort of talk about like, no, no, no, I don't want to get in your way and vice versa.

1309
01:01:19.760 --> 01:01:29.600
I want you to note at 9 minutes, 28 seconds, while Dwight and Andy are talking, Aaron is in the background directly in the middle of these two guys.

1310
01:01:30.120 --> 01:01:31.920
Oh, I'm sure that was on purpose.

1311
01:01:32.300 --> 01:01:33.000
Oh, it was.

1312
01:01:33.200 --> 01:01:34.960
Gene and Lee said that was intentional.

1313
01:01:35.420 --> 01:01:43.240
They said they did this as many times as they could in this episode because it is a story about a woman coming between two guys.

1314
01:01:43.700 --> 01:01:49.600
I really loved Leslie's look in the background as well.

1315
01:01:49.740 --> 01:01:51.500
There's a lot to see in the background of the scene.

1316
01:01:51.620 --> 01:01:52.240
That's pretty great.

1317
01:01:52.460 --> 01:01:55.340
And there's also someone missing in the background of the scene.

1318
01:01:56.180 --> 01:01:57.200
Where is Jim?

1319
01:01:57.200 --> 01:02:00.340
I can tell you where he was.

1320
01:02:00.520 --> 01:02:01.140
Where was he?

1321
01:02:01.460 --> 01:02:05.480
They shared in the commentary that John had to leave early to be on The Tonight Show.

1322
01:02:05.700 --> 01:02:06.840
Oh, my gosh.

1323
01:02:08.040 --> 01:02:15.580
Well, you know, we were rapidly approaching our 100th episode of The Office, which is going to be Company Picnic, the finale of Season 5.

1324
01:02:15.580 --> 01:02:19.240
And we were starting to do a lot of press and promotion for that.

1325
01:02:19.560 --> 01:02:32.240
I saw on the call sheets that after work on Thursday of this week, me and John and Rain stayed after work and we shot some syndicated promos.

1326
01:02:32.240 --> 01:02:32.880
Oh, yeah.

1327
01:02:33.140 --> 01:02:38.060
I found some old emails that a few of us did a satellite media tour as well.

1328
01:02:38.260 --> 01:02:38.740
I bet.

1329
01:02:38.960 --> 01:02:39.080
Yeah.

1330
01:02:39.440 --> 01:02:45.640
I always got roped in for those and they started at four in the morning because you do East Coast to West CoaSt.

1331
01:02:45.880 --> 01:02:47.220
We were very excited.

1332
01:02:47.360 --> 01:02:48.360
We were happy to do it.

1333
01:02:48.480 --> 01:02:49.340
We were team players.

1334
01:02:49.640 --> 01:02:51.960
I was always really proud of our group effort for the show.

1335
01:02:51.960 --> 01:02:59.660
Well, Jim is going to reappear pretty quickly because he's asking Oscar what the rundown is, right?

1336
01:02:59.840 --> 01:03:03.520
He's gone over to the accounting nook much the way that Michael used to do.

1337
01:03:03.680 --> 01:03:08.580
He would go ask Oscar what something meant and now Jim is doing it.

1338
01:03:08.720 --> 01:03:11.320
I mean, Oscar's kind of the smartest guy in The Office.

1339
01:03:11.680 --> 01:03:16.120
Jenna, I love that you said that because Justin Spitzer said this in the commentary.

1340
01:03:16.520 --> 01:03:19.940
He joked that Oscar was the voice of the writers.

1341
01:03:19.940 --> 01:03:23.440
Of course, he's the smartest guy who's always judging everyone.

1342
01:03:26.900 --> 01:03:28.020
Yeah, 100%.

1343
01:03:28.020 --> 01:03:30.560
But Oscar says, why don't you just ask him?

1344
01:03:30.740 --> 01:03:33.300
Just ask Charles what the rundown is.

1345
01:03:34.140 --> 01:03:39.100
So there was a deleted scene where Jim actually took Oscar's advice.

1346
01:03:39.300 --> 01:03:39.480
What?

1347
01:03:39.800 --> 01:03:40.140
Yeah.

1348
01:03:40.460 --> 01:03:41.380
You've got to hear it.

1349
01:03:44.010 --> 01:03:44.550
You have a second?

1350
01:03:44.910 --> 01:03:45.790
What is it, Jim?

1351
01:03:46.050 --> 01:03:47.250
It's about the rundown.

1352
01:03:47.630 --> 01:03:52.070
Jim, God, this rundown is taking more of my time than if I did it myself.

1353
01:03:52.070 --> 01:03:52.510
What?

1354
01:03:53.490 --> 01:03:54.530
What is the question now?

1355
01:03:55.550 --> 01:03:56.250
What's a rundown?

1356
01:03:58.670 --> 01:03:59.690
Is this one of your pranks?

1357
01:04:04.020 --> 01:04:04.180
Huh?

1358
01:04:05.940 --> 01:04:06.260
Yep.

1359
01:04:08.260 --> 01:04:08.580
Boom.

1360
01:04:08.840 --> 01:04:09.040
Jim.

1361
01:04:09.360 --> 01:04:09.620
Sorry.

1362
01:04:09.820 --> 01:04:10.320
I don't have time.

1363
01:04:10.400 --> 01:04:10.640
I know.

1364
01:04:10.820 --> 01:04:10.940
Okay.

1365
01:04:11.120 --> 01:04:11.360
All right.

1366
01:04:11.600 --> 01:04:12.500
I'm going to get you that rundown.

1367
01:04:12.520 --> 01:04:13.240
Just give it to me, Jim.

1368
01:04:13.380 --> 01:04:13.680
Right now.

1369
01:04:13.980 --> 01:04:16.440
I'm going to go out and find it.

1370
01:04:17.240 --> 01:04:18.560
Oh, my gosh.

1371
01:04:18.820 --> 01:04:19.740
Isn't that amazing?

1372
01:04:20.080 --> 01:04:24.900
And I love that Charles clearly knows that Jim's the prankster, which he probably, you

1373
01:04:24.900 --> 01:04:27.560
know, just add that to the list of things he doesn't like about Jim.

1374
01:04:27.840 --> 01:04:30.940
But Jim actually asked him and then failed.

1375
01:04:31.860 --> 01:04:33.640
I bet that was a really funny scene.

1376
01:04:33.640 --> 01:04:34.680
I wish that had stayed in.

1377
01:04:34.920 --> 01:04:35.640
It was great.

1378
01:04:35.740 --> 01:04:38.660
There was so much awkward, just long pauses.

1379
01:04:39.000 --> 01:04:39.180
Oh.

1380
01:04:39.820 --> 01:04:44.540
Well, back downstairs, Michael determines that their office space is too small.

1381
01:04:45.500 --> 01:04:49.520
He says that the solution is for Pam and Ryan to each choose a corner.

1382
01:04:50.080 --> 01:04:52.060
Pam suggests they work from home.

1383
01:04:52.360 --> 01:04:55.740
Ryan suggests Michael fire whichever of them has less education.

1384
01:04:56.200 --> 01:04:58.440
There's a little bit of that passive aggressive.

1385
01:04:58.980 --> 01:05:02.060
But Michael is like, no, my corner idea is what it is.

1386
01:05:02.300 --> 01:05:08.800
I want you to know there was a talking head in the script where Michael says that he negotiated

1387
01:05:08.800 --> 01:05:10.860
a seven-year lease on this space.

1388
01:05:11.140 --> 01:05:11.420
No.

1389
01:05:13.560 --> 01:05:14.920
But it gets worse.

1390
01:05:15.280 --> 01:05:18.740
He says, originally, Billy started at three years.

1391
01:05:19.100 --> 01:05:20.840
Michael countered with seven.

1392
01:05:21.020 --> 01:05:22.020
No, Michael.

1393
01:05:22.380 --> 01:05:24.520
And then Michael says, I should have said 10.

1394
01:05:26.180 --> 01:05:30.040
And so this is going to be their space for seven years.

1395
01:05:30.720 --> 01:05:32.140
Oh, my gosh.

1396
01:05:32.940 --> 01:05:34.360
Justin pointed out something really funny.

1397
01:05:34.560 --> 01:05:39.220
He was like, you know, when Michael says there are four corners in this room and you guys

1398
01:05:39.220 --> 01:05:40.840
kind of look to camera like, yeah, idiot.

1399
01:05:41.840 --> 01:05:43.680
Actually, there were more than four.

1400
01:05:43.960 --> 01:05:47.720
There were because there were some like weird bumpy things.

1401
01:05:49.560 --> 01:05:52.040
Well, Pam is going to retreat to her corner.

1402
01:05:52.260 --> 01:05:56.940
By the way, her corner is next to the sewage pipe and the shower.

1403
01:05:57.140 --> 01:05:58.380
Facing a wall.

1404
01:05:58.540 --> 01:06:00.300
You'd think it can't get worse.

1405
01:06:00.780 --> 01:06:03.660
Ryan's corner is like behind a plant.

1406
01:06:03.660 --> 01:06:05.900
It's actually kind of the nicest corner.

1407
01:06:07.060 --> 01:06:11.960
But things are going to get worse for Pam because Michael says that's his corner because he can't

1408
01:06:11.960 --> 01:06:14.660
work in the same corner that he relaxes in.

1409
01:06:15.000 --> 01:06:16.740
So she's like, which one's mine?

1410
01:06:16.880 --> 01:06:18.880
And he says, yours is the one over there.

1411
01:06:19.100 --> 01:06:20.460
By the copier.

1412
01:06:20.620 --> 01:06:25.280
Oh, we had a fan catch at 12 minutes, one second.

1413
01:06:25.600 --> 01:06:27.840
And it's a great continuity catch.

1414
01:06:28.000 --> 01:06:28.960
It's very subtle.

1415
01:06:28.960 --> 01:06:36.460
So hats off to Tatiana V, who says, when Pam goes to sit in her corner, she takes a small

1416
01:06:36.460 --> 01:06:38.020
black object with her.

1417
01:06:38.200 --> 01:06:43.260
You can see her holding it in her lap as the camera swings back and forth from her and Michael.

1418
01:06:44.760 --> 01:06:51.120
But right before she gets up to leave, it has disappeared from her hands because Pam is

1419
01:06:51.120 --> 01:06:52.900
now holding the arms of her chair.

1420
01:06:53.200 --> 01:06:54.100
What is it?

1421
01:06:54.320 --> 01:06:55.840
That's what she wanted to know.

1422
01:06:56.120 --> 01:06:57.960
It was Pam's flip phone.

1423
01:06:57.960 --> 01:07:01.380
Pam grabs her flip phone off of the poker table.

1424
01:07:01.520 --> 01:07:05.820
But clearly, I didn't do it in every take because it does just vanish.

1425
01:07:06.340 --> 01:07:07.700
I miss my flip phone.

1426
01:07:08.300 --> 01:07:08.980
You do?

1427
01:07:09.200 --> 01:07:09.600
I do.

1428
01:07:09.740 --> 01:07:14.220
And I miss the little antenna it had and how I would close the antenna with my chin.

1429
01:07:14.600 --> 01:07:15.860
I'd like shove it into my chin.

1430
01:07:16.340 --> 01:07:17.960
It did feel fun.

1431
01:07:18.160 --> 01:07:19.080
I loved it.

1432
01:07:19.220 --> 01:07:19.270
The flip phone.

1433
01:07:19.440 --> 01:07:19.580
Yeah.

1434
01:07:20.160 --> 01:07:25.060
Well, you know, Samsung has a new flip phone thing where you flip it open and it becomes

1435
01:07:25.060 --> 01:07:26.040
like a big screen.

1436
01:07:26.040 --> 01:07:27.580
Have you seen the commercials for it?

1437
01:07:27.580 --> 01:07:28.660
I'll never be able to figure it out.

1438
01:07:28.820 --> 01:07:29.780
There's too many moving parts.

1439
01:07:29.980 --> 01:07:30.420
I know.

1440
01:07:30.560 --> 01:07:31.800
But it looks cool in the commercials.

1441
01:07:31.840 --> 01:07:33.040
It really does, Samsung.

1442
01:07:33.540 --> 01:07:35.640
You know what I don't miss about my flip phone, lady?

1443
01:07:35.880 --> 01:07:36.160
What?

1444
01:07:36.380 --> 01:07:39.260
I don't miss the texting where you had to...

1445
01:07:39.260 --> 01:07:42.700
A, A, B, B, B, C, C, D, D, E, E.

1446
01:07:42.840 --> 01:07:44.060
Like you had to click, click, click.

1447
01:07:44.120 --> 01:07:44.170
Yeah.

1448
01:07:45.540 --> 01:07:52.060
Listen, all of this business with Ryan and the corners, Pam's going to leave.

1449
01:07:52.280 --> 01:07:56.280
She goes upstairs and she asks Charles for her old job back.

1450
01:07:56.600 --> 01:07:58.600
She doesn't consult her fiance.

1451
01:07:59.320 --> 01:08:01.620
Not that she needs to consult him, but you know what I mean?

1452
01:08:01.660 --> 01:08:02.920
You would think she'd loop him in.

1453
01:08:03.080 --> 01:08:06.060
You'd think she'd like say, Jim, I'm going to ask for my job back.

1454
01:08:06.400 --> 01:08:10.400
But she didn't consult him when she quit and she's not going to consult him now.

1455
01:08:10.620 --> 01:08:11.420
She's desperate.

1456
01:08:11.580 --> 01:08:13.040
She doesn't have time for that conversation.

1457
01:08:13.260 --> 01:08:13.400
No.

1458
01:08:14.000 --> 01:08:15.940
Well, Charles says the position has been filled.

1459
01:08:16.340 --> 01:08:18.060
She says maybe a sales job.

1460
01:08:18.180 --> 01:08:19.980
Maybe a job as his personal assistant.

1461
01:08:20.780 --> 01:08:21.580
Personal shopper.

1462
01:08:22.360 --> 01:08:22.940
Nope.

1463
01:08:23.180 --> 01:08:24.080
No dice.

1464
01:08:24.900 --> 01:08:31.520
So Justin talked about several different alts in the scene where they had Charles be really

1465
01:08:31.520 --> 01:08:37.620
sort of abrupt with Pam and they dialed it back because it seemed too harsh.

1466
01:08:37.780 --> 01:08:39.000
So he's just more indifferent.

1467
01:08:39.280 --> 01:08:40.060
He's just more business.

1468
01:08:40.780 --> 01:08:40.940
Yeah.

1469
01:08:41.180 --> 01:08:47.260
Well, this was my only real one-on-one scene with Idris, except for when he sort of came

1470
01:08:47.260 --> 01:08:49.860
in the first day, but that wasn't much of an exchange.

1471
01:08:50.540 --> 01:08:51.820
I was so nervous.

1472
01:08:52.700 --> 01:08:54.020
I was such a fan.

1473
01:08:54.580 --> 01:09:00.300
And to be standing there with this actor that I admired so much, because I was a huge fan

1474
01:09:00.300 --> 01:09:00.840
of The Wire.

1475
01:09:01.100 --> 01:09:05.580
And he has such a patient, quiet power in his scenes.

1476
01:09:05.780 --> 01:09:05.960
Mm-hmm.

1477
01:09:06.340 --> 01:09:07.760
And he's such a pro.

1478
01:09:08.040 --> 01:09:16.840
I mean, I was just, I think some of my nervousness as Pam was just my nervousness as Jenna performing

1479
01:09:16.840 --> 01:09:18.360
with this person that I admired.

1480
01:09:18.360 --> 01:09:18.920
Yeah.

1481
01:09:19.480 --> 01:09:23.660
Word has clearly gotten out about the Michael Scott Paper Company being downstairs because

1482
01:09:23.660 --> 01:09:27.460
Phyllis and Stanley decided to go pop by and say hi.

1483
01:09:27.620 --> 01:09:28.740
We really know what it was.

1484
01:09:28.880 --> 01:09:29.800
They were just snooping.

1485
01:09:30.460 --> 01:09:31.280
Oh, yeah.

1486
01:09:31.380 --> 01:09:31.580
Yeah.

1487
01:09:31.680 --> 01:09:32.560
I would do the same thing.

1488
01:09:32.560 --> 01:09:33.080
Are you kidding?

1489
01:09:33.580 --> 01:09:39.960
Well, at the top of the scene, when Phyllis and Stanley poked their head in, I want you

1490
01:09:39.960 --> 01:09:43.200
to notice that Michael is playing with the stapler.

1491
01:09:43.960 --> 01:09:48.120
The stapler that we loved, that none of us could keep our hands off of.

1492
01:09:48.320 --> 01:09:53.180
We would seriously staple papers on our desk.

1493
01:09:53.320 --> 01:09:56.760
So do you think Steve was just like playing with the stapler he thought was cool?

1494
01:09:57.500 --> 01:10:01.740
Because I don't know how to explain this air pressure mechanism of the stapler.

1495
01:10:01.880 --> 01:10:02.020
Okay.

1496
01:10:02.100 --> 01:10:04.900
Next time I'm over at your house, will you just show me the stapler?

1497
01:10:04.900 --> 01:10:07.400
I seriously should have brought it in because you can hear it.

1498
01:10:07.500 --> 01:10:13.160
It's like, it's like having all the power of an industrial stapler.

1499
01:10:13.440 --> 01:10:14.980
With the palm of your hand.

1500
01:10:15.140 --> 01:10:16.680
